---
import { ArrowLeft, ArrowUpRight, Download, Copy, Check } from '@lucide/astro';
import examples from '../../data/examples.json';
import { highlight } from '../../lib/highlight';
import '@fontsource-variable/geist';
import '@fontsource-variable/geist-mono';
import '../../styles/global.css';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Run the Kedi movie example with a TMDB lookup tool and typed captures."
    />
    <title>Movie night example - Kedi</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/assets/kedi-favicon.webp" type="image/webp" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="guide-header">
      <a href="/" aria-label="kedi home" class="brand">
        <img
          class="brand-logo"
          src="/assets/kedi-logo.svg"
          width="64"
          height="44"
          alt=""
        />
        <span>kedi</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href="/">
        <ArrowLeft size={16} /> Back to the homepage
      </a>
    </header>
    <main class="example-guide">
      <h1>Movie night</h1>
      <p class="guide-intro">
        Find a film by name, call TMDB through a tool, and capture its director,
        release year, and runtime as typed values.
      </p>
      <section aria-labelledby="files-title">
        <h2 id="files-title">1. Get the program</h2>
        <p>
          Download the program into your project directory. Its movie lookup
          tool is supplied by the{' '}
          <a href="https://registry.kedi-lang.org/package/tmdb">
            tmdb registry package
          </a>
          .
        </p>
        <div class="downloads">
          <a class="text-link" href="/examples/movie_night.kedi" download>
            <Download size={16} /> movie_night.kedi
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="setup-title">
        <h2 id="setup-title">2. Prepare the environment</h2>
        <p>
          In a uv project with Python 3.11 or newer, install Kedi and the Google
          model provider:
        </p>
        <div class="guide-command">
          <div class="command-title">
            <span>INSTALL DEPENDENCIES</span>
            <button
              type="button"
              data-copy-guide
              aria-label="Copy dependency install command"
              title="Copy command"
            >
              <Copy size={16} class="copy-icon" />
              <Check size={16} class="copied-icon" />
            </button>
          </div>
          <pre><code>uv add kedi 'pydantic-ai-slim[google]'</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>Add the TMDB package to your Kedi registry:</p>
        <div class="guide-command">
          <div class="command-title">
            <span>INSTALL PACKAGE</span>
            <button
              type="button"
              data-copy-guide
              aria-label="Copy TMDB install command"
              title="Copy command"
            >
              <Copy size={16} class="copy-icon" />
              <Check size={16} class="copied-icon" />
            </button>
          </div>
          <pre><code>uv run kedi add tmdb</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>
          The package installs its HTTPX dependency into the same environment.
          See the{' '}
          <a href="https://registry.kedi-lang.org/package/tmdb">tmdb package</a>{' '}
          and the{' '}
          <a href="https://docs.kedi-lang.org/getting-started/installation/">
            Kedi installation guide
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="keys-title">
        <h2 id="keys-title">3. Configure your keys</h2>
        <p>
          In that directory, create a local <code>.env</code> with your Google
          API key and your TMDB <strong>API Read Access Token</strong>. The TMDB
          token is sent as a Bearer header; it is not the shorter API key.
        </p>
        <pre><code>GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-google-api-key
TMDB_API_KEY=your-tmdb-read-access-token</code></pre>
        <p>
          Keep <code>.env</code> out of version control. The keys are used by
          your local program, never by this website.{' '}
          <a href="https://developer.themoviedb.org/docs/getting-started">
            TMDB setup <ArrowUpRight size={13} />
          </a>
        </p>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="run-title">
        <h2 id="run-title">4. Run the program</h2>
        <div class="guide-command">
          <div class="command-title">
            <span>RUN</span>
            <button
              type="button"
              data-copy-guide
              aria-label="Copy run command"
              title="Copy command"
            >
              <Copy size={16} class="copy-icon" />
              <Check size={16} class="copied-icon" />
            </button>
          </div>
          <pre><code>uv run kedi movie_night.kedi --adapter-model google/gemini-3-flash-preview</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>
          The model can call <code>movie_details</code> to search for the title
          and read its details. The template binds three values; the final
          statement returns the director. Model and TMDB requests use your
          accounts.
        </p>
        <div class="code-body">
          <pre><code>{examples.hello.code.split('\n').map(line => <span class="guide-code-line">{highlight(line).map(token => <span class={token.kind ? `syntax-${token.kind}` : undefined}>{token.text}</span>)}{'\n'}</span>)}</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>
          For a remake or an ambiguous title, include its release year in the
          template. The tool accepts a year and rejects ambiguous matches.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <script>
      const copyTimers = new WeakMap<HTMLButtonElement, number>();
      document
        .querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy-guide]')
        .forEach((button) => {
          button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
            const code = button
              .closest('.guide-command')
              ?.querySelector('code');
            if (!code) return;
            try {
              await navigator.clipboard.writeText(code.textContent ?? '');
              window.clearTimeout(copyTimers.get(button));
              button.classList.add('is-copied');
              button.title = 'Copied';
              copyTimers.set(
                button,
                window.setTimeout(() => {
                  button.classList.remove('is-copied');
                  button.title = 'Copy command';
                }, 1600),
              );
            } catch {
              const range = document.createRange();
              range.selectNodeContents(code);
              window.getSelection()?.removeAllRanges();
              window.getSelection()?.addRange(range);
            }
          });
        });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  .guide-header,
  .example-guide {
    width: min(820px, calc(100% - 40px));
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .guide-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 20px;
    padding-block: 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .example-guide {
    padding-block: 48px 80px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 42px;
  }
  .guide-intro {
    margin-top: 18px;
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  section {
    margin-top: 38px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 22px;
    text-wrap: initial;
  }
  p {
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  p a {
    color: var(--green-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  p svg {
    display: inline;
    vertical-align: middle;
  }
  pre {
    margin-top: 18px;
    padding: 18px;
    background: var(--white);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .guide-command {
    margin-top: 18px;
    border: 1px solid #9aa69b;
    background: var(--white);
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .command-title {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 7px 10px 7px 14px;
    background: #e3e8e2;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #aeb9ae;
    font: 11px/1.4 var(--mono);
    color: #43574c;
  }
  .command-title button {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 30px;
    height: 30px;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
  }
  .command-title button:hover,
  .command-title button:focus-visible {
    background: #d2dfd2;
  }
  .guide-command pre {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 14px;
    border: 0;
    overflow-x: auto;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    font: 13px/1.7 var(--mono);
  }
  .downloads {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 12px 28px;
    margin-top: 18px;
  }
  .code-body {
    margin-top: 20px;
  }
  .code-body pre {
    margin: 0;
    border: 0;
  }
  .guide-code-line {
    white-space: pre-wrap;
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    h1 {
      font-size: 34px;
    }
    .example-guide {
      padding-top: 32px;
    }
  }
</style>
